═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  RESULTS — Three Service Concerns Demonstration
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Storage (Flexo Layer 0 + Layer 1):
    Accepted ALL operations without complaint.
    Every SPARQL INSERT/DELETE was valid RDF.
    Storage is indifferent to semantic meaning.

  Schema (Ontology Packages):
    Two packages loaded as composable modules:
      kc-core:    abstract topological backbone
      mtg-domain: domain-specific extension (depends on kc-core)
    The same pattern applies to SysML v2:
      KerML:      core modeling abstractions
      SysML ext:  discipline-specific extensions

  Verification (Constraint Service):
    Client-side verification successfully:
      - Validated ancestor state (PASS)
      - Validated individual commits (both PASS)
      - Detected invalid merged state (FAIL on branch-uv)
    The verification gate pattern shows where enforcement belongs.

  Key finding:
    Independently valid commits can produce invalid merged states.
    Storage cannot detect this — it accepts any valid RDF.
    Schema defines what 'valid' means (ontology + shapes).
    Verification checks it. All three concerns are necessary.

  Compare branch-uv vs branch-vu for non-commutativity.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
